join cook left
if {cook_introduced} == false:
	set {cook_introduced} = true
	join detective right
	detective: Hello.
	join cook left
	cook: Hey.
	detective: I'm here to ask you some questions about the murder.
	cook: I figured.
	detective: Mind introducing yourself?
	cook: My name is [COOK]. I make food for Dracula. Or, did, rather.
	cook: It was about time though, honestly. The guy's been around for way too long.
	cook: But now some other sucker is going to take his place for the next 400 years until the same happens to them.
	detective: You don't like Dracula very much, do you?
	cook: It's nothing personal. Vampires in general get under my skin.
	cook: In the metaphorical sense, that is.
	detective: Yet you work for one?
	cook: Someone has to pay my bills, and I don't know if you noticed, but Drac's pretty loaded— er, was.
	detective: Anyway, moving on.
	detective: What can you tell me about the murder?
	cook: The dinner party was just wrapping up. I was exhausted.
	cook: I thought I was done for the night, but [NIECE] ordered up one last round of Drac's favorite dessert. So I got to work.
	cook (unamused): Ugh.
	cook (speaking): Anyway, a few minutes after, the guy collapsed out of the blue.
	cook: [NIECE] and [FRIEND] came to his aid, brought him upstairs.
	cook: That was the last time I saw him.
	cook: ...
else:
	if {cook_angry} == false:
		cook: Hello.
	else:
		cook (squinting): What do you want?
- Present evidence
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"present_evidence":"cook"}"]
- Leave
